 "verses": {
  "bsb|GEN 15:6": {
   "text": "Abram believed the LORD, and it was credited to him as righteousness."
  },
  "bsb|GEN 16:15": {
   "text": "And Hagar bore Abram a son, and Abram gave the name Ishmael to the son she had borne."
  },
  "bsb|GEN 16:16": {
   "text": "Abram was eighty-six years old when Hagar bore Ishmael to him."
  },
  "bsb|GEN 17:24": {
   "text": "So Abraham was ninety-nine years old when he was circumcised,"
  },
  "bsb|GEN 17:26": {
   "text": "Abraham and his son Ishmael were circumcised on the same day."
  },
  "bsb|ROM 4:10": {
   "text": "In what context was it credited? Was it after his circumcision, or before? It was not after, but before."
  },
  "bsb|ROM 4:11": {
   "text": "And he received the sign of circumcision as a seal of the righteousness that he had by faith while he was still uncircumcised. So then, he is the father of all who believe but are not circumcised, in order that righteousness might be credited to them."
  },
  "bsb|ROM 4:9": {
   "text": "Is this blessing only on the circumcised, or also on the uncircumcised? We have been saying that Abraham’s faith was credited to him as righteousness."
  },
