   "text": "In the selfsame day was Abraham circumcised, and Ishmael his son."
  },
  "kjv|ROM 4:10": {
   "marked": "How was it then reckoned? when he was in circumcision, or in uncircumcision? Not in circumcision, but in uncircumcision.",
   "text": "How was it then reckoned? when he was in circumcision, or in uncircumcision? Not in circumcision, but in uncircumcision."
  },
  "kjv|ROM 4:11": {
   "marked": "And he received the sign of circumcision, a seal of the righteousness of the faith which [he had yet] being uncircumcised: that he might be the father of all them that believe, though they be not circumcised; that righteousness might be imputed unto them also:",
   "text": "And he received the sign of circumcision, a seal of the righteousness of the faith which he had yet being uncircumcised: that he might be the father of all them that believe, though they be not circumcised; that righteousness might be imputed unto them also:"
  },
  "kjv|ROM 4:9": {
   "marked": "[Cometh] this blessedness then upon the circumcision [only], or upon the uncircumcision also? for we say that faith was reckoned to Abraham for righteousness.",
   "text": "Cometh this blessedness then upon the circumcision only, or upon the uncircumcision also? for we say that faith was reckoned to Abraham for righteousness."
  },
  "lat|GEN 15:6": {
   "text": "Credidit Abram Deo, et reputatum est illi ad justitiam."
  },
  "lat|GEN 16:15": {
   "text": "Peperitque Agar Abræ filium: qui vocavit nomen ejus Ismaël."
  },
  "lat|GEN 16:16": {
   "text": "Octoginta et sex annorum erat Abram quando peperit ei Agar Ismaëlem."
  },
  "lat|GEN 17:24": {
   "text": "Abraham nonaginta et novem erat annorum quando circumcidit carnem præputii sui."
  },
  "lat|GEN 17:26": {
   "text": "Eadem die circumcisus est Abraham et Ismaël filius ejus:"
  },
  "lat|ROM 4:10": {
   "text": "Quomodo ergo reputata est? in circumcisione, an in præputio? Non in circumcisione, sed in præputio."
  },
  "lat|ROM 4:11": {
   "text": "Et signum accepit circumcisionis, signaculum justitiæ fidei, quæ est in præputio: ut sit pater omnium credentium per præputium, ut reputetur et illis ad justitiam:"
  },
  "lat|ROM 4:9": {
   "text": "Beatitudo ergo hæc in circumcisione tantum manet, an etiam in præputio? Dicimus enim quia reputata est Abrahæ fides ad justitiam."
  }
